## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* Python (Automation & orchestration)
* Docker (Container runtime)
* PostgreSQL (Data persistence)
* Nginx (Traffic control & logging)
* GitHub Actions — Self-Hosted (CI/CD)
* Linux (Hardened environment)

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Requirements

* Linux host (Ubuntu/Debian recommended)
* Docker & Docker Compose
* Python 3.x
* SSH configured with keys

### Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/jeanlucndato/IRONSTACK-Hardened-On-Prem-Automation-Framework.git
cd IRONSTACK-Hardened-On-Prem-Automation-Framework
```

```bash
docker-compose up -d
```

```bash
python infra_manager.py --config config.yaml
```

---

## 🧩 Key Engineering Decisions

### Why On-Prem?

Because some environments simply cannot trust the cloud.

### Why Python?

For flexibility, readability, and rapid automation.

### Why Self-Hosted CI/CD?

To ensure deployment pipelines remain **within the trust boundary**.

---

## 📈 Future Evolution

IRONSTACK is designed as a foundation.

Next steps include:

* Multi-node orchestration
* Monitoring stack (Prometheus / Grafana)
* Security scanning (containers & configs)
* Advanced alerting system
* Integration with vulnerability management tools

